## Concept Overview
A closure is a fundamental JavaScript concept where an inner function maintains access to variables in its outer (lexical) scope, even when the outer function has completed execution. This creates a private scope for data encapsulation.

## Implementation Details
- Closures are created automatically when functions are defined inside other functions
- The inner function retains a reference to the outer function's variables
- This enables private variables and methods, similar to object-oriented encapsulation
- Memory is managed automatically - closures persist as long as references exist

## Code Example
```javascript
function createCounter() {
  let count = 0; // Private variable

  return {
    increment: function() {
      count++; // Accesses outer scope variable
      return count;
    },
    decrement: function() {
      count--;
      return count;
    },
    getCount: function() {
      return count;
    }
  };
}

const counter = createCounter();
console.log(counter.increment()); // 1
console.log(counter.increment()); // 2
console.log(counter.getCount());  // 2
```

## Common Pitfalls
- **Memory leaks**: Closures can prevent garbage collection if references persist unnecessarily
- **Loop confusion**: Variables in closures capture by reference, not value (use `let` or IIFE)
- **Performance impact**: Creating many closures can affect memory usage
- **`this` binding**: Arrow functions don't have their own `this`, which affects closure behavior

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design a robust per-key caching layer with concurrency control and real-time updates, mirroring production frontend concerns in large apps.

## Key Concepts

- Closure-based state encapsulation
- Deduplicating concurrent async calls
- In-flight concurrency control and queuing
- Per-key TTL caching
- Real-time update propagation into cache

## Code Example

```javascript
function createPresenceCache(fetchPresence, { ttl = 30000, maxInFlight = 5, onUpdate } = {}) {
  const cache = new Map();
  const inFlight = new Map();
  const waitQueue = [];

  function drain() {
    if (inFlight.size >= maxInFlight || waitQueue.length === 0) return;
    const next = waitQueue.shift();
    if (!next) return;
    const { userId, resolve } = next;
    const p = fetchPresence(userId).then(status => {
      cache.set(userId, { status, expires: Date.now() + ttl });
      if (onUpdate) onUpdate(userId, status);
      inFlight.delete(userId);
      resolve(status);
      drain();
      return status;
    }).catch(err => { inFlight.delete(userId); throw err; });
    inFlight.set(userId, p);
  }

  async function getPresence(userId) {
    const cached = cache.get(userId);
    if (cached && cached.expires > Date.now()) return cached.status;
    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
      waitQueue.push({ userId, resolve, reject });
      drain();
    }).then(status => status);
  }

  function clear(userId) {
    cache.delete(userId);
  }

  return { getPresence, clear };
}
```

